---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Radical Process">

  <!-- ── HEADER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <header class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-14 pb-4">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <img src="/img/logo.png" alt="Radical Process" class="h-9 w-auto shrink-0" />
      <p class="text-xs uppercase text-gray-500">
        <span class="tracking-[0.45em] text-gray-200">Radical Process</span>
        <span class="text-gray-500 tracking-[0.25em]">
          &nbsp;—&nbsp; Unapologetically niche, unapologetically deep
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ── SGD ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">

    <section class="pt-10">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-black tracking-tighter mb-1">SGD</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm tracking-wide uppercase">
          Spatial Gesture Designer &nbsp;·&nbsp; VST3 / AU / Standalone &nbsp;·&nbsp; macOS &amp; Windows
        </p>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-8">
          <a href="#"
             class="block border border-gray-700 hover:border-gray-400 px-6 py-5 text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors">
            <span class="block text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">Download for macOS</span>
            <span class="block text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2 tracking-wide uppercase">
              Apple Silicon &nbsp;·&nbsp; VST3 / AU / Standalone
            </span>
          </a>

          <div class="border border-gray-800 px-6 py-5 text-gray-600">
            <span class="block text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">Windows</span>
            <span class="block text-xs mt-2 tracking-wide uppercase">Coming soon</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-4 tracking-wide uppercase">
          14-day free trial &nbsp;·&nbsp; every feature unlocked &nbsp;·&nbsp; no registration
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        SGD turns a sound file into a <em class="not-italic text-white">gesture</em>: a sound together with its
        motion through a virtual room around the listener. You draw the path on the room floor, lift it into
        three dimensions with an elevation curve, bend the timing with a motion curve, and bind the result to a
        MIDI key. Pressing that key does not merely play the sound, it sends it travelling — around you,
        overhead, past your ear.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        SGD does not pan. It binauralizes every gesture against a physical model of the room, so on headphones
        the sound leaves your head, with distance, air, wall reflections and Doppler all following from the space
        you built. The whole spatial computation runs offline in the background, so playback itself costs almost
        nothing — and every gesture still keeps its own mixer strip with gain, three-band EQ and a send to the
        shared room reverb.
      </p>

      <figure class="mb-16">
        <video src="/video/sgd-digest.mp4"
               poster="/img/sgd-digest-poster.jpg"
               autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"
               aria-label="A silent screen recording of SGD: drawing a gesture's path on the room floor, shaping its elevation curve, and watching the gestures fly through the room from outside."
               class="w-full border border-gray-800"></video>
        <figcaption class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3">
          Edit view — the whole instrument on one screen: gestures on the left, the room floor in the middle,
          the curve editor below it, and the keyboard they all play from along the bottom. Drawing a path,
          shaping its curves, sizing the room, then out to the observe view.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- ── PITCHES ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-14 mb-16">

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-gesture.png" alt="The gesture list: each row shows a key dropdown, the gesture name, its sound file and length, and a thumbnail of its path."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">A sound, a path, a key</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            That is a gesture, and the list keeps all three together: the sound file it plays, a thumbnail of the
            path it flies, and the key it answers to. Pick a new key from the dropdown and the binding moves with
            it — up to 128 gestures in a room, each with its own colour.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-key.png" alt="The keyboard strip: coloured dots on C4, D4, E4 and the black keys mark the gestures bound to each key."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Play space like an instrument</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Every gesture lives on a MIDI key, marked by its own colour on the keyboard. Spatial sound design
            stops being an automation-lane chore and becomes something you perform live, from your DAW or the
            standalone application.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-trajectory.png" alt="The trajectory editor: a looping path drawn around the listener with the sample's waveform painted along it."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Draw the motion, sculpt the time</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The waveform is painted along the trajectory, so you see which part of the sample happens where. The
            motion curve then lets the source rush, hesitate, freeze mid-air, or run the path backwards.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-elevation.png" alt="The elevation editor: breakpoints above and below the listener's ear line define the height of the path."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Lift it off the floor, stretch it wide</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            One editor, three curves. Elevation lifts the path over your head or drops it to your feet; the
            width curve spreads the two channels of a stereo file apart like wingtips, opening from a point into
            a wide wash and closing again.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-render.png" alt="The render panel: Direct plus first, second and third order reflections, a Doppler amount knob, and a background render progress bar."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Sound that leaves your head</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            True binaural rendering, with distance, air absorption and up to three orders of wall reflections.
            Dial the reflections deeper for dense, vivid spaces, and set the Doppler shift of moving sources to
            taste.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-room.png" alt="The room settings dialog: a wireframe room with the listener at its centre, size in metres, and wall material controls."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Rooms are real, and they are yours</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Width, height and depth in metres, with a wall material of your choice — absorption, damping,
            scatter and RT60. Resize the room or swap concrete for carpet and the reflections, the reverb and
            every gesture adapt automatically. Rooms save as self-contained folders, samples included.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-mix.png" alt="The per-gesture mix strip: gain, low, mid and high EQ knobs, and a send to the shared room reverb."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Every gesture keeps its own strip</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Gain, three-band EQ and a send to the shared room reverb, per gesture. Nothing is ever rendered
            twice: reopen a room and it is instantly ready; tweak a curve and only that one gesture quietly
            re-renders while you keep working.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-trim.png" alt="The trim dialog: a stereo waveform with a highlighted region and fade handles at each edge."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Only the part that flies</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Drag over the waveform to keep the part of the sound you want, pull the triangles for fades, and
            slide the whole region along the file. The gesture and its painted trajectory redraw around whatever
            you keep.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <figure>
        <img src="/img/sgd-observe.png" alt="The SGD observe view: the room as a wireframe box seen from outside, with four named gestures tracing coloured paths around the listener."
             class="w-full border border-gray-800" />
        <figcaption class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3">
          Observe view — the room from outside at true scale, the listener at its centre, every sounding gesture
          named and tracing its path in its own colour, each with a glowing sphere that swells and fades with the
          loudness of the sound.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SPECS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mt-20 border-t border-gray-900 pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-500 mb-6">Specs</h2>

      <dl class="text-sm border-t border-gray-900 mb-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Platform</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">macOS, Apple Silicon (ARM) only</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Formats</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">VST3, AU, Standalone</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Sample rates</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">44.1, 48 and 96 kHz only</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The macOS build runs on Apple Silicon (ARM) only — there is no Intel build, and it will not run on
        Intel Macs, including under Rosetta. Sessions must run at 44.1, 48 or 96 kHz; other sample rates are
        not supported.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── TRIAL & LICENCE ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mt-20 border-t border-gray-900 pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-500 mb-6">Trial &amp; licence</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        SGD starts with a <strong class="font-medium text-white">free 14-day trial</strong>. The trial is the
        complete plugin: every feature is unlocked for the whole period, with no watermark, no export limit and
        nothing held back. Starting it takes one click — no name, no email address, no registration.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        When the 14 days are over, SGD keeps running and your rooms keep opening, but the plugin is
        <strong class="font-medium text-gray-300">muted</strong> — it produces no audio output until a valid
        licence key is entered. Enter one at any time, before or after the trial ends, and the sound comes
        straight back. One key covers every machine you own — see
        <a href="/licensing" class="text-gray-300 underline underline-offset-4 decoration-gray-700 hover:text-white transition-colors">how licensing works</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-gray-900 text-center text-gray-600 text-xs py-10 tracking-widest uppercase">
    <p>
      <a href="/about" class="hover:text-gray-400 transition-colors">About</a>
      <span class="text-gray-800 mx-2">·</span>
      <a href="/licensing" class="hover:text-gray-400 transition-colors">Licensing</a>
      <span class="text-gray-800 mx-2">·</span>
      <a href="/privacy" class="hover:text-gray-400 transition-colors">Privacy</a>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">&copy; 2026 Radical Process. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>

</Layout>
